content.text:
Right, Rust doesn't have default parameters. Common patterns:

**Option approach:**
```rust
pub fn print_summary_header(title: &str, width: Option<usize>) {
    let w = width.unwrap_or(SUMMARY_WIDTH);
    // ...
}
// Called: print_summary_header("TITLE", None) or Some(60)
```

**Explicit const at call site:**
```rust
pub const SUMMARY_WIDTH: usize = 40;

pub fn print_summary_header(title: &str, width: usize) { ... }
// Called: print_summary_header("TITLE", SUMMARY_WIDTH)
```

**Macro (if you really want default syntax):**
```rust
macro_rules! print_summary_header {
    ($title:expr) => { print_summary_header_impl($title, SUMMARY_WIDTH) };
    ($title:expr, $width:expr) => { print_summary_header_impl($title, $width) };
}
```

The `Option` approach is probably cleanest for this case - callers pass `None` for default, `Some(n)` for custom. Which do you prefer?

Nothing specific for simple divider lines - the crates focus on colors ([ansi_term](https://crates.io/crates/ansi_term), [colored](https://crates.io/crates/colored)) or full tables ([comfy-table](https://lib.rs/crates/comfy-table)).

For ~15 lines of code, a dependency seems overkill. Here's the macro approach:

```rust
pub const SUMMARY_WIDTH: usize = 40;
pub const SUMMARY_CHAR: char = '=';

macro_rules! print_header {
    ($title:expr) => { $crate::print_header_impl($title, SUMMARY_WIDTH, SUMMARY_CHAR) };
    ($title:expr, $width:expr) => { $crate::print_header_impl($title, $width, SUMMARY_CHAR) };
    ($title:expr, $width:expr, $ch:expr) => { $crate::print_header_impl($title, $width, $ch) };
}

macro_rules! print_footer {
    () => { $crate::print_footer_impl(SUMMARY_WIDTH, SUMMARY_CHAR) };
    ($width:expr) => { $crate::print_footer_impl($width, SUMMARY_CHAR) };
    ($width:expr, $ch:expr) => { $crate::print_footer_impl($width, $ch) };
}

pub fn print_header_impl(title: &str, width: usize, ch: char) {
    let line: String = std::iter::repeat(ch).take(width).collect();
    println!();
    println!("{}", line);
    println!("{:^width$}", title, width = width);
    println!("{}", line);
    println!();
}

pub fn print_footer_impl(width: usize, ch: char) {
    let line: String = std::iter::repeat(ch).take(width).collect();
    println!("{}", line);
    println!();
}
```

Usage:
```rust
print_header!("TEST SUMMARY");           // defaults
print_header!("TEST SUMMARY", 50);       // custom width
print_header!("TEST SUMMARY", 50, '-');  // custom width + char
```

